   "subject": "Making a genetic map in a BC2S3 population",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello all,</div><div><br></div>I have been attempting to make a genetic map using <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px\">Gen</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">=read.cross (</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px\">format</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(158,0,3)\">&quot;csv&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px\">file</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(158,0,3)\">&quot;file&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px\">BC.gen</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">2</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px\">F.gen</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">3</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px\">estimate.map</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(181,118,12)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.9px;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">)</span><div><br></div><div> After completing the mapping all of my markers are evenly spaced 10 cM. I have limited recombination in the population and I think that the BCsFt Tools for R/qtl would be robust enough to handle my population structure and markers.</div><div><br></div><div>I have 159 individuals and roughly 151 polymorphic markers.  I have been attempting to map 1 chromosome at a time.</div><div><br></div><div>Maybe because of the limited recombination I am unable to accurately estimate the cM values for the markers in this population?</div><div><br></div><div>Has anyone experienced and issue like this?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Sean</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
